.TH "COOKIESTOREMANAGER.SUBSCRIBE" "3JS" "April 22, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CookieStoreManager.subscribe \- CookieStoreManager: subscribe() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Service Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]subscribe()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]CookieStoreManager\f[R] interface subscribes a
\f[CR]ServiceWorkerRegistration\f[R] to cookie change events.
.PP
Duplicate subscriptions are ignored: that is, if a service worker
subscribes more than once to the same cookie, it will only receive each
change notification once.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
subscribe(subscriptions)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]subscriptions\f[R]
An array of objects, each of which has the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]name\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string equal to the name of a cookie.
If \f[CR]name\f[R] is omitted, the service worker is subscribed to
change events for all cookies that are in scope.
.TP
\f[B]url\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string equal to the URL of a cookie scope.
This may be narrower than the scope of the service worker registration.
If \f[CR]url\f[R] is omitted, it defaults to the scope of the service
worker registration.
.RE
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with \f[CR]undefined\f[R] when the
subscription completes.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if the \f[CR]url\f[R] is not a valid URL, or doesn\(cqt start
with the service worker registration\(cqs \f[CR]scope\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Setting name and URL
In this example, the \f[CR]ServiceWorkerRegistration\f[R] represented by
\f[CR]registration\f[R] is subscribing to change events on the cookie
named \f[CR]\(dqcookie1\(dq\f[R] with a scope of
\f[CR]\(dq/path1\(dq\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Subscribe to a specific cookie and URL\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] subscriptions = [{ name: \(dqcookie1\(dq, url: \(ga/path1\(ga }];
\f[B]await\f[R] registration.cookies.subscribe(subscriptions);
.EE
.SS Setting name only
In this example, we set only \f[CR]name\f[R] and omit \f[CR]url\f[R]:
the subscription applies to all cookies named \f[CR]cookie1\f[R] within
the service worker\(cqs scope.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Subscribe to all cookies named \(dqcookie1\(dq in the registration scope\f[R]
\f[B]await\f[R] registration.cookies.subscribe([{ name: \(dqcookie1\(dq }]);
.EE
.SS Setting URL only
In this example we set only \f[CR]url\f[R], and omit \f[CR]name\f[R]:
the subscription applies to all cookies within the specified URL scope.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Subscribe to all cookie changes within a specific path\f[R]
\f[B]await\f[R] registration.cookies.subscribe([{ url: \(dq/path/one/\(dq }]);
.EE
.SS Subscribing to all cookies
In this example, both \f[CR]name\f[R] and \f[CR]url\f[R] are omitted.
The subscription applies to all cookies within the service worker\(cqs
scope.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Subscribe to all cookie changes within the entire registration scope\f[R]
\f[B]await\f[R] registration.cookies.subscribe([{}]);
.EE
.SS Setting a URL outside the service worker\(cqs scope
If the URL is outside the service worker\(cqs scope,
\f[CR]subscribe()\f[R] will throw a \f[CR]TypeError\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]Bad\f[R]
.IP
.EX
\f[B]await\f[R] registration.cookies.subscribe([
  { name: \(dqcookie1\(dq, url: \(dq/out\-of\-scope/\(dq },
]);
.EE
